WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.420
- I wanted to mention something

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:03.120
'cause I used a GIF of you.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.050
Because I love you, and it's funny.

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:08.350
So, I was having the worst day ever.

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:11.010
Literally, my dryer broke,
my clothes ended up,

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.540
we have no clothesline,
so I just had to hang them

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:14.500
on the back porch area.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.430
And they flew off into the forest,

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:18.390
and I had to go find all of them.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:20.390
And, anyway, it was a really rough day.

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:21.223
And then, I got back in

00:00:21.223 --> 00:00:23.150
and I had all these
texts, and they were like,

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:24.320
Man, so now there's Murder Hornets.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:25.710
And I was like, "Wait, what?"

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.150
And I started looking up

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:28.800
what the hell a Murder Hornet was.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.880
And then I, anyway, I used
your GIF that was like, "Sure."

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.880
Like, of course this
is happening, why not?

00:00:37.059 --> 00:00:37.892
- Yeah.

00:00:37.892 --> 00:00:40.170
- Have you heard of Murder Hornets?

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:44.180
- No, I mean, I was, this weekend,

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:46.330
reading a newspaper article about it.

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:47.760
And again, it was just
one of those things,

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.350
we did a thing on our show
called, Not Now, Murder Hornets,

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.830
which is, we don't have the bandwidth

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:54.440
to be worried about you at this moment.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:55.970
- (laughs loudly)

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:58.750
- If you were looking to make
a splash, Murder Hornets,

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:00.290
you picked the wrong time, I think.

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:03.060
You need to do it before,
or after, a pandemic,

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.050
in the middle of it.

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:07.080
I think there are people
who are, at this point,

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:09.950
would be terrified about Murder
Hornets at any other time

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:12.010
that are now like, "Great,
whatever. Bring it on.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:13.690
Let's just have it all at once."

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:16.620
- I'm honestly, and this happened
to me the other day, too.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:19.930
There was an earthquake here,
and I didn't know earthquakes

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:21.170
happened in Montana.

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:25.050
And I was just like, when
are the locusts coming?

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:25.883
- Yeah.

00:01:25.883 --> 00:01:29.160
- Everything is just going to crap.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:30.300
I don't know what's happening.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:32.430
And it's not, that was a bad day.

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:34.540
But, anyway, I just thought it was funny.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:36.630
'Cause they're called
Murder Hornets, apparently,

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:38.810
because they decapitate honey bees.

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:40.850
They just take their head off.

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:42.340
Which I was like, of course we would have

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:44.490
something called a
Murder Hornet right now.

